Description:FIELD OF INVENTION
The present invention relates to parking management. More specifically, the present invention relates to an IoT Based Smart Parking Availability Tracker & Billing System. 
BACKGROUND
The increasing urbanization of cities worldwide has resulted in a growing demand for efficient parking management systems. As cities become more densely populated, finding available parking spaces has become a significant challenge, contributing to congestion, increased fuel consumption, and elevated emissions. Traditional parking systems, which often rely on manual monitoring or static signage, are ill-equipped to handle the dynamic nature of modern urban environments, leading to inefficient use of space and frustrating drivers. The inefficiencies of traditional parking systems also have broader environmental implications, particularly in urban centers where air quality and traffic-related pollution are already major concerns.
US20110080304A1 discloses a method for parking a vehicle in a parking spot comprises the steps of: providing a vehicle having a sensing system and a park assist system, the sensing system including a sensor which provides an input signal; scanning neighbouring objects to determine if a feasible target parking space is available; determining whether there is a sufficient slot length in which to park the vehicle and calculating a trajectory path to guide the vehicle into the space; starting a parking manoeuvre; deactivating the assist system by a driver/passenger action; storing the parking information determined above; and requesting a driver command to resume the parking manoeuvre, wherein if the driver selects to resume the parking manoeuvre the assist system uses the stored parking information to guide the vehicle into the space.
The existing invention lacks accuracy in identification the empty parking space and vehicle in parking space. The installation cost of the existing invention is high. Hence there is need for the present invention.
OBJECTIVE OF THE INVENTION
The main objective of the present invention is to manage parking space.
Another objective of the present invention is to provide a cost-effective system for parking management without the need for heavy equipment.
Yet another objective of the present invention is to provide real-time information about the empty parking space to the vehicle driver.
Yet another objective of the present invention is to design a parking system with minimum electronic hardware requirement with scope of increasing scalability. 
Yet another objective of the present invention is to provide navigation assistance to the general vehicle to reach the empty parking space.
Yet another objective of the present invention is to provide automated billing for parking.
Yet another objective of the present invention is to c.
SUMMARY OF THE INVENTION
The present invention relates to an IoT Based Smart Parking Availability Tracker & Billing System. The present invention includes a primary node, a slave node, a personal computing device, and a backend server. The primary node is affixed to the parking lot. The primary node includes a primary node camera. The primary node camera captures the video of the space in the parking lot, herein, the primary node functions as a bird's-eye view camera with help of the primary node camera, thus providing continuous real-time monitoring of the parking lot to maintain an accurate tally of parking lot occupancy. The slave node is connected to the primary node and is only triggered upon detection of change in the parking lot occupancy by the primary node. The slave node includes a slave node camera. The slave node camera captures the image of the number plate of the vehicle entering and exiting the parking lot, thus helps in identifying the vehicle for tracking and billing, wherein, the captured image of number plate is being sent to the primary node by the slave node.  The primary node and the slave node are system on chip computer module. The personal computing device is being used by a driver of a vehicle for navigation to parking lot, bill payment, live video feed of the vehicle and notifications. The personal computing device of the driver of the vehicle receives navigation data from the backend server that is used by the driver of the vehicle to reach the parking lot. The backend server is connected to the primary node, and the personal computing device of the driver of the vehicle. The backend server includes a database and a processor. The database stores live video of the parking lot, data of vehicle, billing data, data of the drivers of the vehicle, computer readable instructions, and pre-trained artificial intelligence models. Herein, the backend server receives the video of the parking lot in real-time and number plate image of the vehicles in the parking lot from the primary node and the slave node, and the backend server executes the computer readable instructions that use the pre-trained artificial intelligence models to identify an accurate tally of parking lot occupancy and as well as identifies number plate of the vehicle entering and exiting the parking lot, thus helps in identifying the vehicle for tracking and billing, then the backend server sends live video feed, notifications, timeline of parking, and bill to the personal computing device.
The main advantage of the present invention is that the present invention has designed a parking system with minimum electronic hardware requirement with the scope of increasing scalability.
Another advantage of the present invention is that the present invention uses artificial intelligence for identification of vehicles and management of parking spaces.
Yet another advantage of the present invention is that the present invention provides real-time information about the empty parking space for the vehicle driver.
Yet another advantage of the present invention is that the present invention provides automated billing and a payment system for parking. 
Yet another advantage of the present invention is that the present invention sends real-time alerts to users through the mobile app, notifying them when their session begins and ends, providing convenience and ensuring accurate billing and users also receive alerts about the status of their parking space.
Yet another advantage of the present invention is that the present invention generates immediate alerts and ensures timely warnings about proximity to potential road congestion and hazards.
The objectives, advantages, and features of the present invention will become apparent from the detailed description provided herein below, in which various embodiments of the disclosed invention are illustrated by way of example.
BRIEF DESCRIPTION OF THE DRAWINGS
The accompanying drawings are incorporated in and constitute a part of this specification to provide a better understanding of the invention. The drawings illustrate one embodiment of the invention and together with the description, explain the principles of the invention. 
Fig. 1 illustrates an IoT Based Smart Parking Availability Tracker & Billing System. 
