Complete Specification

Description:FIELD OF THE INVENTION:
The present invention relates to field of Medicinal Chemistry and Drug Discovery. Particularly, the present invention provides novel pyrazole derivatives linked to 4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate. The invention also provides a process for the preparation of these novel pyrazole derivatives linked to 4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate.

BACKGROUND OF THE INVENTION:
Over the past decade, there has been a significant increase in interest in pyrazole chemistry, primarily driven by the discovery of fascinating properties demonstrated by numerous pyrazole derivatives. Pyrazoles, as five-membered heterocycles, belong to a class of compounds highly valued in organic synthesis. Within the azole family, they are among the most extensively studied groups of compounds. Over the years, a vast array of synthesis methods and synthetic analogues have been documented, highlighting their significant importance in research and applications. Furthermore, the pyrazole fragment plays a crucial role in numerous organic ligands and serves as an essential coordinator. Recent research has uncovered intriguing applications of the pyrazole structure in organic synthesis, where it acts as both a directing and transforming group. Pyrazole serves as a fundamental element present in various small molecules, exhibiting a diverse array of agricultural and pharmaceutical activities. Specifically, they are classified as inhibitors of protein glycation, exhibiting properties such as anti-inflammatory, antibacterial, antifungal, anticancer, antidiabetic, antioxidant, antidepressant, anti-tuberculosis, and antiviral activities. Additionally, certain pyrazoles find applications in supramolecular and polymer chemistry, in the food industry, and are utilized as cosmetic colorings. In recent years, a number of FDA-approved and commercially available drugs, both patented and non-patented, have been formulated using pyrazole derivatives. This trend highlights the extensive utilization of these groups in the creation of novel bioactive compounds. Some of the prior art disclosing the pyrazole and thiazole derivatives have been listed below.

WO2012099915A1 discloses deuterated thiazolidine derivatives and compositions comprising these compounds, which are useful agents for the treatment of hyperglycemia diseases or disorders, in particular diabetes mellitus. The disclosure also provides a method of treating hyperglycemia diseases or disorders, in particular diabetes mellitus, using these deuterated thiazolidine derivatives.

US2008021032A1 discloses pyrazole derivatives that act as glucokinase activators and are useful for the treatment of metabolic diseases and disorders, preferably diabetes mellitus, more preferably type II diabetes mellitus.

Most of the pyrazole derivatives disclosed in prior art shows antidiabetic activity. However, these molecules primarily exhibit moderate efficacy in reducing blood glucose levels, often requiring high doses. Furthermore, the pharmacokinetics of these molecules showed poor bioavailability and limited stability in biological systems, leading to rapid metabolism and excretion. Also, these derivatives have moderate efficacy, show off-target effects, have poor solubility, and metabolic instability. Hence, there is a need to design and develop pyrazole derivatives that can efficiently overcome these challenges and are useful in managing diabetes effectively.

OBJECTIVES OF THE INVENTION:
It is an objective of the present invention to provide novel pyrazole derivatives linked to 4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate.

It is another objective of the present invention is to provide a process for the preparation of novel pyrazole derivatives linked to 4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate.

