3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-1-phenyl-1-H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde;
3-(4-methoxyphenyl)-1-phenyl-1-H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde;
3-(2,4-dihydroxyphenyl)-1-phenyl-1-H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde;
3-(3-hydroxyphenyl)-1-phenyl-1-H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde;
3-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)-1-phenyl-1-H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde; and
3-(3-nitrophenyl)-1-phenyl-1-H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde.

The solvent is selected from absolute ethanol and glacial acetic acid.
The crude product is purified by column chromatography on silica with 60-120 mesh using a solvent mixture.

The solvent mixture comprises ethyl acetate and hexane in a ratio of 80:20.

The pyrazole derivative is prepared by a process, comprising:
adding phosphorous oxychloride to a solution of hydrazone in dimethyl formamide at 0-5 °C under stirring for 17-22 minutes to obtain a mixture;
refluxing the mixture at 70-80 oC for 6-8 hours followed by its cooling and quenching; and
neutralizing the quenched mixture with sodium bicarbonate followed by filtering, drying and recrystallizing to obtain the pyrazole derivative.

