Instruments and Materials
Sigma Aldrich and Merck India chemicals, solvents, and reagents were employed to synthesize the compounds. TLC was used to study the reaction on pre-coated Aluminium sheets Silica Gel Merck 60 F254 (Merck) utilizing Toluene: Ethyl acetate: formic acid (5:4:1), benzene: acetone (8:2), and TLC spot visualization using UV light and iodine chamber. Open glass capillary tubes were used to measure the uncorrected melting temperatures of the produced compounds. Infrared (IR) spectra were verified using KBr pellets on an (IR Affinity SHIMADZU) FTIR-spectrophotometer, To obtain proton (1H) and carbon-13 (13C) nuclear magnetic resonance spectra, they were recorded on two different Bruker models (DRX-400 MHz and DMSO-d6) at different frequencies, using tetramethylsilane (TMS) as the internal standard in CDCl3 and DMSO-d6, respectively. Waters mass spectrometer was used to record mass spectra (ESI-m/z). A Perkin-Elmer model 240C was used to analyze the elements (C, H, and N). C, H, and N results.

EXAMPLES:
Having described the basic aspects of the present invention, the following non-limiting examples illustrate specific embodiments thereof. Those skilled in the art will appreciate that many modifications may be made in the invention without changing the essence of invention.

Example 1. Synthesis of (E)-1-phenyl-2-(1-phenylethylidene)hydrazine (IIIA-P).
In a 100 mL round-bottomed flask, a mixture of substituted acetophenones (IA-P) (0.01 M) and (II) phenylhydrazine (0.02 M) were dissolved in absolute ethanol (20-25 mL) and refluxed for 6-7 hours. After completion, the absolute ethanol was evaporated in vacuum, the solid product was transferred to crushed ice with constant stirring, filtered, and washed with chilled GAA and cold water, dried and recrystallized with ethanol to give the molecule (IIIA-P) as mentioned in scheme 1.

Example 2. Synthesis of 1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde (IVA-P).
The substituted hydrazones (IIIA-P) (0.188 M) were dissolved in DMF and POCl3 (0.0385 M) was gradually added to it at 0-5 °C with continuous stirring followed by stirring at room temperature for 17-22 minutes. The reaction mixture was refluxed at 70-80 oC for 6-8 hours. As the reaction was complete, the reaction mixture was allowed to attain the room temperature and crushed ice was added to it. The reaction mixture was neutralized with a saturated solution of NaHCO3. The solid product was filtered, dried and recrystallized with ethanol which gave the desired yield (IVA-P) as mentioned in scheme 1.

Example 3. Synthesis of ethyl 2-amino-4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate (3).
In a round bottom flask, thiourea (0.098 mM) (1), was dissolved in anhydrous ethanol (70 mL) and ethyl-2-chloro acetoacetate (0.097 mM) (2) was added drop-wise with constant stirring at room temperature. Once addition of ethyl-2-chloro acetoacetate was complete, reaction mass was refluxed at 80-90oC for 3-4 hrs. After completion of the reaction, the reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature and the solid precipitate was isolated, washed with cold ethanol and further washed with saturated sodium bicarbonate solution, filtered, dried and recrystallized with ethanol to obtain the white solid molecule (3) as mentioned in scheme 1.

Example 4. Synthesis of ethyl 2-(((1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)amino)-4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate (VA-P).
To the solution of 3-(-4-substituted phenyl)-1-phenyl-1-H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde (IVA-P); (1 mM) in absolute ethanol (30 mL), ethyl 2-amino-4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate (2 mM) and GAA (1 mL) was added. The reaction mixture was refluxed at 50-60oC for 6-8 hours. As the reaction was complete, the reaction mass was cooled to room temperature and the solid precipitate was isolated, filtered and evaporated under a vacuum to afford the crude product which was purified by using column chromatography on silica (60-120 mesh) using ethyl acetate/hexane (80:20) to give the final molecules (VA-P) as mentioned in scheme 1.

