Spectral features of synthesized molecules
As presented in Scheme I, phenylhydrazine hydrate II was prepared by refluxing substituted acetophenone IA-P in the presence of absolute ethanol and glacial acetic acid. The substituted (E)-1-phenyl-2-(1-phenylethylidene)hydrazines IIIA-P obtained, was further cyclized using POCl3 and DMF to form the respective substituted 1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde products IVA-P. The intermediate product ethyl 2-amino-4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate 3 was obtained by the reaction of thiourea and 2-chloroethylacetoacetate. The final molecules VA-P were obtained by the reaction of intermediate molecule 3 (2mM) and IVA-P in presence of catalytic amount of glacial acetic acid. 

The formation of Ethyl-2-(((1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)amino)-4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate derivatives VA-P was confirmed by 1H NMR spectra, showed the characteristic peak for CH=N proton in the range of d 8.46?9.11 ppm, and a broad singlet for CH3 at d 2.41?2.49 ppm. The proton of pyrazole ring appeared as a singlet in the region of d 8.42?8.51 ppm. In 13C NMR C=N carbon peaks appeared at d 160 ppm and all aromatic carbon peaks appeared in the region of d 119.2?163.0 ppm. The IR spectra of VA-P showed C=N stretching at 1449?1521, C?H aromatic stretching at 3029? 3357, and C?N stretching at 1335?1373 cm-1, C=O stretching at 1745?1762cm-1, C?S 667?712 cm-1. The molecular weight of the molecules was confirmed by the mass spectra.

A pictorial representation of spectral features of novel molecule Ethyl-2-(((1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)amino)-4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate (VA) is given in figure 1. , Claims:1. A 4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate linked pyrazole derivative compound of structural formula (1):


Formula (I)

wherein the compound is a pyrazole derivative linked to 4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate,
and wherein R = H, 4-bromo, 2-bromo, 4-fluoro, 2-fluoro, 4-methyl, 2-methyl,4- chloro, 2,4- dichloro,4- hydroxy, 3- hydroxy,2,4 dihydoxy, 4-methoxy, 2,5-dimethoxy,3-nitro, 4-nitro.

2. The compound as claimed in claim 1, wherein the compound of structural formula (1) is selected from the compounds:
Ethyl-2-(((1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)amino)-4-methylthiazole-5-carboxylate;
